97
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:10,550
So there's a great phrase here in Fluency Builder that we use when we're trying to be polite in English.

98
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:13,870
Michelle says oh hi Jeremy please go ahead.

99
00:05:14,470 --> 00:05:21,370
Okay so Jeremy asks if she needs to use the photocopier and he said no Jeremy it's okay go ahead.

100
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:22,250
Please go ahead.

101
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:33,230
This literally means you go ahead of me but in reality she's basically saying I can wait you go first.

102
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:41,520
So if you're going into a building and somebody opens the door before you and they say please go ahead.

103
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:43,390
That means they'll hold the door and you can go inside first.

104
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,490
So please go ahead.

105
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:51,230
This is a very polite thing to do and if you're in line and you see someone is in a hurry you can say this to them please go ahead.

106
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,720
Alright very good.

107
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,150
Please go ahead.

108
00:05:54,720 --> 00:06:00,750
And we also going back to the contract discussed about confirming the deal.

109
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,480
Okay.

110
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:08,580
So you have a deal or an agreement or a contract but the thing you do to make sure that you all agree is you confirm.

111
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,580
So this means you want to make sure it is actually going to happen.

112
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:27,660
And you can actually combine confirm with many different things like you can confirm your tickets to go to Italy or can we confirm those holidays before I make my bookings because I want to go to Italy.

113
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,560
Exactly.

114
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:36,580
So you confirm something and then Jeremy said a very strange phrase here fingers crossed after talking about the deal.

115
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,600
Okay so fingers crossed is an interesting phrase.

116
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:56,200
It doesn't mean okay now go cross your fingers but it's something we say to be superstitious because it means basically I hope so or hopefully because fingers crossed when you cross your fingers in many Anglo-American cultures you are saying that you hope something will happen.

117
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,840
It's to bring good luck.

118
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:02,280
So oh gosh I really hope it doesn't rain today.

119
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,110
And then I say fingers crossed.

120
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,970
Yeah well fingers crossed it doesn't.

121
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:09,490
That means that we hope it doesn't but now that you said that maybe it will.

122
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,040
Right.

123
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:22,520
So I think it's kind of a superstitious belief that people have that if you cross your fingers it will bring good luck or what you say will happen will happen or won't happen.

124
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,330
That's right fingers crossed.

